2026-10-23T10:11:43.7529337Z Linux USB/IP device management (experimental preview)
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7529764Z 
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7529928Z Usage: rustusb [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7530230Z 
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7530356Z Commands:
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7530851Z   physical-pending    Inspect unresolved physical grants through the root helper (root only)
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7531588Z   physical-reconcile  Verify restored physical state and retire its grant record (root only; no USB writes)
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7532601Z   physical-server     Serve explicitly authorized whole USB devices through Linux USBFS (experimental, no TLS)
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7533883Z   virtual-server      Serve two virtual test devices; this experimental mode provides no authentication or TLS
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7535227Z   devices             Scan local devices without changing drivers. Discovery is not compatibility validation
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7535929Z   doctor              Read installed tool, module and helper capabilities without loading modules
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7536538Z   discover            Query a server's USB/IP device list over an administrator-managed trusted network
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7537203Z   export              Export an administrator-allowlisted device fingerprint via the privileged helper
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7538054Z   unexport            Release an allowlisted export and request local driver reattachment
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7538587Z   attach              Import a remote bus ID through an allowlisted endpoint and Linux VHCI
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7539059Z   detach              Disconnect an authorized local VHCI port (0..255)
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7539523Z   sessions            Read authoritative native kernel session state through the helper
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7539964Z   status              Query helper and kernel status
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7540342Z   help                Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7540614Z 
2026-10-23T10:11:43.7540695Z Options:
